Chapter: ElfStdio
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

Section: Body

 THE PAYLOAD LEADS WITH A MODE BYTE, the way the pe plug's does: 0 is a
 bootable bare-metal image, 1 is a user-mode ELF64 at the conventional Linux
 base, and 2 is a HOSTED CONSOLE ELF built from a whole CDX. One target, three
 containers, chosen by the caller rather than by which plug got built.

 Mode 2 takes the CDX WHOLE rather than the unpacked wire the other two take,
 because the hosted container needs the entry offset out of the CDX header and
 that is not in the wire. It is the same payload shape the pe plug already
 uses, and the parsing is the plug's rather than the caller's.

 An unknown mode is REFUSED by name and not absorbed by a fallback. A front
 door whose `otherwise` accepts anything makes a setting that does nothing
 look exactly like one that works, and here the thing that looks like it
 worked is a downloadable binary (L-ACCEPTED, and the same reason
 `compile-plain` names TEXT rather than falling through to it).

  plug-emit-bytes : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  plug-emit-bytes (payload-buf) (payload-len) =
   if payload-len < 13 then print-line-uni ("REFUSED short payload " & show payload-len)
   else if list-at (__buf-read-bytes payload-buf 0 1) 0 == 2 then
    if payload-len < 225 then print-line-uni ("REFUSED mode 2 payload " & show payload-len & " is shorter than a CDX header")
    else write-binary (build-elf64-console-from-cdx payload-buf 1 (payload-len - 1))
   else let cce-table = build-cce-to-ascii-table cce-to-unicode-table
   in let hp = __heap-save
   in let hdr-bytes = __buf-read-bytes payload-buf 0 13
   in let mode = list-at hdr-bytes 0
   in let code-len = read-i32-le hdr-bytes 1
   in let data-len = read-i32-le hdr-bytes 5
   in let func-count = read-i32-le hdr-bytes 9
   in let hr = __heap-restore hp
   in let code-off = 13
   in let data-off = code-off + code-len
   in let func-off = data-off + data-len
   in if func-off > payload-len then print-line-uni ("REFUSED payload " & show payload-len & " shorter than its own header claims " & show func-off)
   else if mode == 0 then
    let funcs = parse-func-table-from-buf payload-buf func-off func-count
    in write-binary (build-elf-from-payload payload-buf code-len data-len code-off data-off (funcs.names) (funcs.offsets) cce-table)
   else if mode == 1 then
    write-binary (build-elf64-user-from-payload payload-buf code-len data-len code-off data-off)
   else print-line-uni ("REFUSED unknown mode " & show mode & ": 0 is a bare-metal image, 1 is a user-mode ELF64, 2 is a hosted console ELF, and nothing else is implemented")
